@plane z=0 label="Context"
The spec stays `specs/generator/generator.spec.md`.

Deterministically scaffolds spec files and companion files for unspecced modules using built-in or project-owned templates.

This plane is context. Later planes are lessons, in the order they were learned.
`context.md` stays beside this file.

@plane z=1 label="Key Decisions"
- Generation is deterministic and local.
- Custom templates override built-ins without overwriting existing files.
- Companion creation and module discovery remain independent of coding-agent enrichment.
- CLI generate holds one project-root capability through template reads, directory creation, and
  no-overwrite publication; public-path checks detect replacement but never authorize writes.

@plane z=2 label="Files to Read First"
- `src/generator.rs`
- `src/exports/mod.rs`
- `src/types.rs`

@plane z=3 label="Current Status"
Stable local scaffold generator with no provider, credential, network, or shell path. CLI
publication is capability-relative and cannot follow a later public-root redirect.

This module owns what a generated scaffold looks like, and callers asking "has this module
recorded anything, or is it still the template" must ask here rather than keeping their own copy
of the prompt strings. `validator.rs` holds such a copy of three of the four context bullets and
it has already drifted — it omits the Notes bullet — which is the concrete cost of the second
copy rather than a hypothetical one.

A defect in scaffold handling is invisible to dogfooding on this repository: all 62 specs already
have authored prose, so no untouched scaffold exists here to trip over. Any affordance keyed on
"has the author written anything yet" needs a fixture that is the real generated artifact,
because the mature repository no longer contains one.

Anything comparing text against a template must compare against the EXPANDED template. The raw
`CONTEXT_TEMPLATE` carries `{module}`, so its `spec:` line can never equal a real companion's, and
a caller comparing against the raw text silently fails to recognise a line it wrote itself. That
mismatch stayed invisible for as long as frontmatter was being stripped before it mattered, and
appeared the instant stripping failed on CRLF — two defects where either alone is silent.

@plane z=4 label="Cargo generation binding (#813)"
Cargo package names do not identify source filenames. Carry manifest source roots from checked coverage into every generation entry point, intersect them with uncovered files, and preserve more specific named bindings even when batch selection narrows the candidate list. Test init then generate on a real fresh crate; a mature repository with authored specs cannot expose this bootstrap failure.

@plane z=5 label="Cargo review corrections (#813)"
A conventional module and a manifest crate with the same name are one owner: combine their measured files. An exact manifest target must outrank a guessed filename owner, while explicit configuration keeps precedence.

@plane z=6 label="Shared source ownership (#813)"
Excluding every source claimed by another target drops shared files from every owner. Independently including directory roots duplicates overlapping owners. Resolve ownership once from the captured manifest: nearest path first, selected names then lexical order for ties. Retain narrower unselected targets during batch generation. An explicit mapping that matches nothing remains authoritative.
